### Semantic colors (forms, dashboard, payments, alerts)

Use these for validation, payment states, live indicators, and app UI — not as brand accents on marketing pages.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--bdgs-success` | `#22C55E` | Success text/icon, live pulse, payment confirmed |
| `--bdgs-success-bg` | `#ECFDF5` | Success field/banner background |
| `--bdgs-success-dark` | `#16A34A` | Success hover / stronger emphasis |
| `--bdgs-error` | `#DC2626` | Validation errors, failed payments, required-field markers |
| `--bdgs-error-bg` | `#FEF2F2` | Error field/banner background |
| `--bdgs-warning` | `#D97706` | Pending states, expiring sessions, soft alerts |
| `--bdgs-warning-bg` | `#FFFBEB` | Warning banner background |
| `--bdgs-info` | `#6366F1` | Informational notices, tooltips, onboarding hints |
| `--bdgs-info-bg` | `#EEF2FF` | Info banner background |

Do not use coral for error states or success green for primary CTAs. Semantic colors communicate state; brand colors communicate identity.

## Typography

- Font (UI/marketing): `'DM Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif`. Weights 300–700 in 100 steps only.
- Font (code/technical): `var(--bdgs-font-mono)` = `'DM Mono', 'Fira Code', ui-monospace, monospace`. Use for API endpoints, transaction IDs, code snippets, hex tokens, and dashboard technical references. Sizes: body `13px`, small `12px`, weight 400–500.
- Desktop scale: H1 46px/700/lh1.12 · H2 34px/700/lh1.2 · H3 22px/700 · body 15–16px/400/lh1.6 · small 12–13px/500 · nav 14px/500.
- **One production type scale site-wide** — no per-page title sizing drift. A page H1 must be the SAME size as the homepage H1 (46px desktop), never a smaller "section" size.

### Fluid type scale — copy this into every page's `:root` (locked)

Headings must be **fluid** with `clamp()` so they render at their final size immediately (no CLS "title dance") and scale smoothly from mobile to 1920 and across 90–200% browser zoom. Do not hard-code heading sizes per page; use these tokens.

> **Use `px`, not `rem`, for font sizes.** Bootstrap 3 sets `html { font-size: 10px }`, so `1rem = 10px` on our pages — `rem`-based font tokens silently render ~37% too small (e.g. `2.875rem` = 28.75px, not 46px). All font tokens below are px-based on purpose.

```css
:root{
  --bdgs-font-sans: 'DM Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
  --bdgs-font-mono: 'DM Mono', 'Fira Code', ui-monospace, monospace;
  --fs-h1: clamp(28px, 20px + 2.2vw, 46px);   /* 28 -> 46px, hits 46 by ~1200px */
  --fs-h2: clamp(24px, 20px + 1.2vw, 34px);   /* 24 -> 34px */
  --fs-h3: clamp(18px, 16px + 0.6vw, 22px);   /* 18 -> 22px */
  --fs-lead: clamp(16px, 14px + 0.6vw, 19px); /* 16 -> 19px lead paragraph */
  --fs-body: 16px;
  --fs-small: 13px;
  --fs-code: 13px;
  --fs-code-sm: 12px;
}
h1{ font-size:var(--fs-h1); font-weight:700; line-height:1.12; letter-spacing:-1px; }
h2{ font-size:var(--fs-h2); font-weight:700; line-height:1.2; letter-spacing:-0.5px; }
h3{ font-size:var(--fs-h3); font-weight:700; line-height:1.3; }
p{ font-size:var(--fs-body); line-height:1.6; }
code, pre, .bdgs-mono{ font-family:var(--bdgs-font-mono); font-size:var(--fs-code); }
```

Rule of thumb: never size layout by "what fits one screen." Size type with the tokens, then let content flow — the page must NOT use `justify-content:center` inside a `100vh`/`min-height:100vh` shell to vertically center a fixed block (that produces small type + big empty top/bottom on large screens and overflow at zoom).

## Spacing / radius / shadow / z / breakpoints

- Spacing (4px base): `4 8 12 16 20 24 28 32 36 40 48 64 80`. All margin/padding/gap land on this scale.
- Radius: xs4 · sm6 · md8 · 10 · lg12 · xl16 · pill20 · full50%.
- Shadow: sm `0 2px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.06)` · md `0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.06)` · lg `0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.08)` · xl `0 24px 70px rgba(26,26,46,.22)` · coral `0 4px 16px rgba(231,77,86,.08–.35)`.
- Z: base0 · card1–6 · sticky100 · header1000.
- Breakpoints (max-width): xs480 · sm768 · md991 · lg1029 · xl1199. Containers: 1240 (nav) · 1100 (wide) · 900 (content).

## Zoom / responsive (hard rules)

- **Never `height` on variable content — use `min-height`.** Avoid `100vh` with capped content.
- No fixed pixel widths on layout containers — `max-width` + fluid `%`/`rem`. Side gutters `padding-inline: clamp(16px, 4vw, 48px)`.
- Grid/Flexbox for layout (absolute only for tooltips/floating badges). `overflow-x:hidden` on body is a symptom — fix the overflowing element.
- Images: `width:100%` + `aspect-ratio` or intrinsic `width`/`height` (prevents CLS). `loading="lazy"` below the fold. Host on ImageKit.
- **Test matrix (must pass, no h-scroll/clip/overlap):** widths 320/375/480/768/1024/1280/1440/1920; zoom 90/100/110/125/150/175/200%; Windows scaling 100/125/150%.

## Accessibility

- WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large/UI). Visible `:focus-visible` ring: `outline:2px solid var(--bdgs-coral); outline-offset:2px` — never remove without a replacement. Suppress mouse ring via `:focus:not(:focus-visible){outline:none}`.
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for all animation. Text zoom to 200% must not break layout.

## Animation

Hover `all .2s`, transforms `all .25s`, cards `cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)`. Lifts `translateY(-1px|-2px)`. Always provide a `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` fallback.

## Performance & Core Web Vitals

Budget (mobile field data, measured on the **live BD domain**, not github.io): **LCP ≤ 2.5s · CLS ≤ 0.1 · INP ≤ 200ms · Lighthouse ≥ 90.**

- **Fonts:** `&display=swap`, `<link rel="preconnect">` to the font host, preload the one hero weight. Set explicit heading sizes (px `clamp`) so the title renders final-size immediately — no CLS "title dance."
- **Images:** always `width`+`height` or `aspect-ratio`; `loading="lazy"` below the fold; ImageKit WebP; `srcset`/`sizes` on the hero image.
- **JS:** defer non-critical scripts; no late CSS that shifts layout; nothing render-blocking above the fold.
- **Measure:** PageSpeed Insights per URL; log score + CWV; fix per page.

## Custom color registry

Colors outside the global palette are allowed only if: (1) scoped to a section selector (not global `:root`), (2) prefixed per section (e.g. `--prm-*`), (3) registered below, (4) never redefining `--bdgs-*`. Promote to global if reused across 3+ files. Unregistered hex = drift; flag it.

