## Do / Don't guidance format

When documenting a visual rule (in this file, in `docs/design-guidelines.html`, or in a PR note), use paired **Do** / **Don't** panels — not prose alone. Format:

| Side | Label color | Content |
|---|---|---|
| **Do** | `--bdgs-success` / `--bdgs-success-bg` | The correct pattern, with a concrete example (token name, class, or short snippet) |
| **Don't** | `--bdgs-error` / `--bdgs-error-bg` | The anti-pattern, with the exact mistake to avoid |

Rules for writing Do/Don't pairs:
1. One rule per pair — never bundle multiple ideas.
2. Prefer a token or class name over abstract advice ("use `var(--fs-h2)`" not "use consistent headings").
3. Don't invent new tokens inside a Do/Don't — only illustrate tokens already defined above.
4. Visual examples in `docs/design-guidelines.html` are the canonical rendered form of these pairs.

Core pairs (always enforce):

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| Use `var(--bdgs-*)` / `var(--fs-*)` tokens | Hard-code hex or px on headings |
| Use `min-height` on variable content | Use fixed `height` on cards/sections with growing copy |
| Size type with fluid `clamp()` tokens | Override heading `font-size` inside media queries |
| Land spacing on the 4px scale | Magic numbers (`17px`, `13px` gaps) |
| Touch targets ≥ 44×44px | 32px icon-only close buttons |
| Semantic colors for form/payment state | Coral for errors or success-green for primary CTAs |

